{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_doc", "label": "Epic 13 \u2014 Operational Readiness MVP Memo", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/gold-epic-13-mvp-2026-05-10.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Engineering (drafted by Claude Sonnet 4.6)", "contributor": null, "rationale": "Defines the smallest Epic 13 that produces real operational value \u2014 working signals and a practiced response, not a six-week initiative \u2014 holding it to the size-S sizing estimate."}, {"id": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_sli_import_commit_latency", "label": "SLI \u2014 Import commit latency p95 < 30s", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gold-epic-13-mvp-2026-05-10.md", "source_location": "\u00a71a", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chosen first because the commit handler is synchronous, 1083 lines and has no timeout guard, so an operator cannot distinguish a 40-second commit from a timed-out one. Measured by adding durationMs to the existing createRouteLogger line and draining Vercel logs to Axiom/Logtail."}, {"id": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_sli_accounting_backlog", "label": "SLI \u2014 Accounting integration backlog < 10 PENDING", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gold-epic-13-mvp-2026-05-10.md", "source_location": "\u00a71b", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PENDING AccountingIntegrationEvent rows are money recorded in the domain model but not posted to the GL; a growing backlog means the retry job is failing silently. The data is already queryable so no new tables are needed."}, {"id": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_sli_fifo_double_link", "label": "SLI \u2014 FIFO double-link incidents (0 per day)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gold-epic-13-mvp-2026-05-10.md", "source_location": "\u00a71c", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Until the FIFO advisory lock lands, a concurrent commit can link one goldPourId to two BuyerReceipt rows. A daily GROUP BY HAVING COUNT(*) > 1 query costs nothing and catches the double-spend before finance reports do."}, {"id": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_slo_import_commit", "label": "SLO \u2014 import commit p95 < 30s for \u2264100 rows", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gold-epic-13-mvp-2026-05-10.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Same SLO reads differently either side of the worker: before Epic 9a a breach means the route is dangerously slow, after it means the job queue is backed up. Error budget of one breach per 30 days; re-baselined post-worker into enqueue p95 < 2s plus job completion p95 < 60s. No Sentry required."}, {"id": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_on_call_rotation", "label": "Gold on-call rotation skeleton", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gold-epic-13-mvp-2026-05-10.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two Domain Backend engineers, one week each, Monday 09:00 handoff naming open incidents, FAILED accounting rows, import volume and SLO breaches. The duty engineer triages and escalates rather than fixing."}, {"id": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_recovery_drill", "label": "First recovery drill \u2014 the partial commit", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gold-epic-13-mvp-2026-05-10.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A 60-minute tabletop over the 487-row May incident with no production systems touched; drills for the other three scenarios are each gated on the epic that ships the model they exercise."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_doc", "target": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_operational_runbook", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-epic-13-mvp-2026-05-10.md", "source_location": "\u00a71, \u00a74", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_doc", "target": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_sli_import_commit_latency", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-epic-13-mvp-2026-05-10.md", "source_location": "\u00a71a", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_doc", "target": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_sli_accounting_backlog", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-epic-13-mvp-2026-05-10.md", "source_location": "\u00a71b", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_doc", "target": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_sli_fifo_double_link", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-epic-13-mvp-2026-05-10.md", "source_location": "\u00a71c", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_doc", "target": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_slo_import_commit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-epic-13-mvp-2026-05-10.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_doc", "target": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_on_call_rotation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-epic-13-mvp-2026-05-10.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_doc", "target": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_2026_05_10_recovery_drill", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-epic-13-mvp-2026-05-10.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_epic_13_mvp_202